Entertainment Weekly has been working  hard not too long ago they gave us our  first look at Aquaman and earlier this  week they gave us our first look at  Shazam but something even more exciting  is that today they gave us a better look  at venom not only did they give us an  awesome brand new photo but they also  gave us Tom Hardy's thoughts on playing  the character the first photo that they  gave us is of doctor Drake and Tom  Hardy's character Eddie Brock strapped  down to a chair without the context of  the situation it's really hard to say  what this is but no doubt it has  something to do with the symbiote it's a  cool picture but let's get on to the  next one  this picture is awesome it's the most  detailed photo that we've got of venom  so far and it's creepy which I love  venom is a violent character he's a  really violent character actually and it  seems like they're going to do him  justice in this movie it seems like Tom  Hardy thinks so as well let's take a  look at some of the things the actor had  to say about playing Eddie Brock slash  venom when interviewed by Entertainment  Weekly Tom Hardy said as far as Marvel  characters I have to say for me venom  looks the coolest that sounds a bit  shallow but I appreciate that he has a  kind of brazen swagger and a zero  Foxtrot attitude he then goes on to say  there's a tragic clown element which I  find funny and is harmonious with some  of the work that I like to do there's  something funny about the circumstances  of having a gift but it's a tragic gift  it's a superpower you don't really want  but at the same time you love it it  makes you feel special  he's a reluctant hero and an antihero  they then go on to talk about the  difference between Jekyll and Hyde and a  werewolf stating that a werewolf is kind  of two different people it's the human  that transforms into the werewolf and  with the case of dr. Jekyll and mr. Hyde  Jekyll and Hyde are again two different  people Jekyll transforms into Hyde but  unlike these characters venom and Eddie  Brock don't really switch back and forth  from one another instead they occupy the  same body at the same time and they have  to learn to coexist  speaking of this Tom Hardy said we  talked a lot about a werewolf and what  it is when you get infected or bit by a  werewolf usually a human gets imbued  with powers or an alien comes from outer  space and has to figure out how to live  on earth but this is really about a  relationship between two people who have  to work together to create this hybrid  symbiotic relationship and the duality  of the role is actually what really  fascinated Tom Hardy into playing the  character he says it's a bit like Ren &amp;  Stimpy you know they have different  sounds I always saw venom as sounding  like a James Brown lounge lizard and  Eddie Brock is kind of a I don't know an  everyday kind of God but he's inherited  this massive ego this beast the result  of this is of course a black and white  hero whose morals are anything but that  of a hero and which Tom Hardy says  there's that biting off heads issue  which is not what you would expect from  say Captain America taking down a crook  so from this interview it sounds like  Venom's gonna be the real deal they're  gonna stick true to the character which  includes the violence  I actually really hope there's a scene  where then a bite somebody's head off so  that's it for the new photos that we've  received and the interview with Tom  Hardy from Entertainment  let me know what you think of the photos  and the interview and what you're most  excited about when venom comes out be  sure to like the video and be sure to  subscribe to my channel so you can stay  up to date on all things Marvel DC and  superhero thank you so much for watching  woof woof  [Music]
 

